{"reference":"Psalms 116","book":"Psalms","chapter":116,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"A Note on Psalm Numbering","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Some Greek and Latin Psalter traditions number this psalm differently from the Masoretic tradition. Their numbering reflects a broader pattern of combining Psalms 9–10 and 114–115, dividing Psalms 116 and 147, and including Psalm 151 beyond the 150-psalm count. When comparing editions, the psalm’s number may therefore need checking.","verse_refs":["Psalms 116:1-19"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_psalms_116_18747ad72760995227769a3c"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]},{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"The Surrounding Psalms","blocks":[{"id":"block_2","text":"The surrounding psalms belong to a wider collection that holds together memories of sanctuary destruction and Babylonian exile with return thanksgiving, festival praise, Torah meditation, and Songs of Ascents oriented toward worship.","verse_refs":["Psalms 113:1-9","Psalms 114:1-8","Psalms 115:1-18","Psalms 117:1-2","Psalms 118:1-29"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_psalms_116_78d344e617dccb6c5057994d"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}